<title>UK: Rank shares drop as Xerox plunges.</title>
<headline>Rank shares drop as Xerox plunges.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-10-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Britain's Rank Group dropped sharply on Friday afternoon, sucked down by a 20 percent fall in Xerox Corp's stock after the U.S. company released third-quarter results below expectations.</p>
<p>Rank, which has a 20 percent stake in Xerox's Rank Xerox office machinery division, was down 13-1/2p at 432-1/2p in mid-afternoon trade with over 1.2 million shares traded. The broader marker was 0.3 percent higher.</p>
<p>&quot;People took a bit of fright at the Xerox share coming off so badly in the States and that knocked Rank over here,&quot; one London marketmaker said.</p>
</text>
